  "$schema": "Pre-POD-311 metadata of every issue command, read off the RUNNING registry object.",
  "$measuredAt": "issue/279-integration 627a3f14fbf0080ef4465661ce4604e44d039b89, before any POD-311 commit",
  "$why": "THE ZERO-BEHAVIOUR-CHANGE ORACLE. POD-311 moved the contract half of the issue registry to @podium/commands. This file is what the registry DECLARED before that move, captured from the live object rather than from source text, and `registry-metadata.oracle.test.ts` re-measures the same shape and asserts it CELL BY CELL. It is committed ahead of the migration on purpose: a snapshot regenerated by the code it is supposed to check is a vacuous green, so the fixture must exist in history before the change it pins. DO NOT REGENERATE IT. A diff here is either a deliberate behaviour change that needs saying out loud, or the regression the file exists to catch.",
  "$cells": "Asserted per command, not in aggregate: kind, action, scope, cli, whether a target extractor is present, what that extractor returns for a fixed probe input, the input schema's zod type name and its sorted key set. Counting commands or counting distinct cells would both stay green if two commands swapped cells.",
